# Accepted misconfigurations. Each entry states why, so the exception is a
# decision on record and not a silenced scanner.

# AVD-AWS-0132 - the catalog bucket does not use a customer managed KMS key.
# The bucket holds public application installers, not secrets. Encryption is
# on (SSE-S3/AES256), TLS is enforced by bucket policy, versioning is enabled
# and every form of public access is blocked. A customer managed key bills per
# key per month and buys nothing for artifacts anyone can download from the
# vendor. Revisit if the catalog ever stores licensed or customer data.
AVD-AWS-0132
